I take the bus to the sports hall.
It is a dark and cold winter evening.
I arrive at a large sports center.
I walk in through the main entrance.
In here, it is bright and warm.
The hall is enormous.
I listen to the loud echo.
I look at the busy courts.
There are many people.
They like to do sports.
Many of them play badminton.
I can clearly hear the shuttlecocks.
People shout and run fast.
They hit them hard.
It looks very fun.
I would also like to play.
I like to be active.
But first I need to find the reception.
I am walking over there now.
